=== day
n: 8
title: Real shows from the internet
subtitle: fetch and APIs
hours: 3 hours
page: index.html
slot: js | js | app.js
file: app.js = js
refs: @page, helpers.js, data.js

--- intro
Yesterday's ShowShelf knew 12 shows. Today it talks to **TVmaze**, a free online database of TV shows. The search box asks TVmaze, the page starts with real shows, and it tells people when it's loading or when something went wrong.

Your code box starts with the finished app from Day 7, tidied into sections. A few lines are new or changed for today; they say **Day 8** in their comments:

- `state.shows` holds the shows on the page. For now it starts with the 12 sample shows from data.js.
- Search-as-you-type is gone: from today the search goes to TVmaze when the form is sent.
- Cards cope with real shows that have no genre or no rating yet.

**No internet?** The Lab answers with saved sample data from TVmaze, so every step works offline too.

