=== step loading
title: Loading...
minutes: 15
slot: js
--- explain
A request can take a second or two on a slow connection. Meanwhile the page looks as if nothing happened, and people click again and again. Always show that something is happening.

The page has a status line for this, under the genres: `<p class="status" id="status" hidden>`.

Where you put the lines matters, because `await` pauses the function in the middle:

```js
async function saveNotes() {
  saveButton.textContent = "Saving…";   // runs straight away
  await sendNotes();                     // waits here
  saveButton.textContent = "Saved";     // runs when sendNotes is done
}
```

> The `…` is one character. Typing three dots `...` is fine too.
--- task
1. At the top, in the Elements section, find the status line: `const statusMessage = document.querySelector("#status");`
2. At the start of `loadShows`, before the `await`: set its text to "Loading shows…" and show it (`hidden = false`). Also hide `emptyMessage`: an old "nothing found" doesn't belong to the new search.
3. After the `await`: hide the status line again.

Search for something and watch closely: the message flashes up while TVmaze answers.
--- hint
Three lines go before `state.shows = await searchShows(term);` and one line goes after it.
--- hint
