- Quotes instead of backticks around a text with `${term}`.
- Setting the text after `render()` is fine too, but setting it outside `try` shows the old word after an error.


=== step start-page
title: Real shows from the start
minutes: 20
slot: js
--- explain
The page still starts with the 12 sample shows from data.js. Time to start with real ones.

TVmaze has a list of all its shows, in pages of 250: `https://api.tvmaze.com/shows?page=0` is the first page. Unlike a search, each item in that list **is** a show, with no `{ score, show }` around it. So you can hand `toShow` straight to `map`:

```js
const names = ["dark", "fleabag"].map(capitalise);   // the same as .map((n) => capitalise(n))
```

We'll use an empty search box to mean "show page 0 again". `trim()` removes spaces at both ends of a text, so a box with only spaces counts as empty too: `"  dark ".trim()` is `"dark"`.

We've added `getShowsPage()` and a new Start section below your code.
